      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:78:3",
      "text": [
        " إِنَّ الْمُؤْمِنَيْنِ إِذَا الْتَقَيَا فَتَصَافَحَا أَدْخَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ يَدَهُ بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمَا وَ أَقْبَلَ بِوَجْهِهِ عَلَى أَشَدِّهِمَا حُبّاً لِصَاحِبِهِ فَإِذَا أَقْبَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ بِوَجْهِهِ عَلَيْهِمَا تَحَاتَّتْ عَنْهُمَا الذُّنُوبُ كَمَا يَتَحَاتُّ الْوَرَقُ مِنَ الشَّجَرِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ibn Fazzal, from Ali Bin Uqba, from Ayoub, from Al Samyda, from Malik Bin Ayn Al Juhny, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The <span class=\"iTxt\">Momineen</span>, when two meet and shake hands, Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic Inserts His<sup>azwj</sup> Hand between their two hands, and Turn by His<sup>azwj</sup> Face towards the one who has more intense love for his companions. So when Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic Turns by His<sup>azwj</sup> Face upon them both, the sins erode from both of them just as the leaves erode from the tree’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Ibn Faddal has narrated from Ali ibn ‘Uqbah from Ayyub from al-Sumayda’ from Malik ibn ‘A’Yun al-Juhni from abu Ja’far (a.s.) who has said the following: ‘When two believing people meet and shake hands Allah, the Most Majestic, the Most Holy, inserts His hand between their hands and faces the one whose love for his brother (in belief) is more intense. When Allah, the Most Majestic, the Most Holy, turns His face to them their sins begin to fall like leaves from trees.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
